Below is the set up I am currently working with per your suggestion.  From looking at the Stan manual you can subset vectors via indexing y[1:30], but since I do have an id vector in the data block, it seems like there should be an easier way.  Rather than subsetting X, I could also calculate mu=X*beta and then try and subset mu based on the id variable?  Sorry if these are silly questions, but I'm still trying to get familiar with Stan's indexing.  Any help you could provide would be much appreciated.

